      "title": "What to know as Israel polls leave Netanyahu, opposition without majority",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/world-news/what-to-know-as-israel-polls-leave-netanyahu-opposition-without-majority-126103000476_1.html",
      "description": "Final election results have been released in Israel, leaving uncertainty since neither Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's bloc nor the main opposition's has a won a majority in parliament.\nWeeks of negotiations to build a majority coalition and name a prime minister likely lie ahead, with another election possible if they fail. One scenario would be Jewish and Arab-led parties opposed to Netanyahu joining forces, a rare and politically controversial move. Another would be some parties that campaigned on ousting Israel's longest-serving prime minister teaming up with him instead.\nBoth possibilities have prompted bitter debate in an already deeply divided country.\nHere's what to know about what comes next:\nFinal results bring weeks of negotiations\n--------------------------------------------\nThe final vote count released by the Central Elections Committee showed Netanyahu's bloc won 53 seats in the 120-member Knesset, well below the 68 seats it had controlled at its peak in the ..",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-30T05:52:04"
    },
